	"id": "coastal-storm",
	"name": "COASTAL STORM \u2014 Ionian Littoral",
	"description": "A two-fleet surface action fought inside a defended littoral, off the south-east corner of Sicily. RED holds the coast: a Bastion-P coastal regiment reaching 300 km with supersonic P-800s, a DF-21D ballistic battery ranging the whole basin from behind the ridge, an EWR feeding both over datalink, a Kara-class surface group screening the cape and two corvette pickets pushed out ahead of it. BLUE (yours) is a US surface action group \u2014 Ticonderoga, Zumwalt and two Burkes \u2014 approaching from seaward, ~90 km out, and it has to fight through the screen before its guns can reach the shore batteries. Both sides fly CAP and maritime strike. The ships mean it: with anti-ship magazines dry they run each other down to gun range rather than sit out of reach.",
